          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+theory"} group theory
            = succeed "-theory," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
            %em crossed homomorphisms
            (Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CrossedHomomorphism"}
            below) is a generalization of that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphisms"} group homomorphisms
            where a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+action"} group action
            – of the
            = succeed "-group" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphisms"} automorphisms
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
            group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            – is incorporated.
          %p
            Crossed homomorphisms are equivalently
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphism"} homomorphic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            out of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semidirect+product+group"} semidirect product group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ⋊
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \rtimes G
            (Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CrossedHomomorphismsAreSplittingsOfTheSemidirectProductGroup"}
            below).
          %p
            This largely explains their relevance in all contexts of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+algebraic+topology"} equivariant algebraic topology
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+differential+topology"} equivariant differential topology
            = succeed "-theory" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+principal+bundle"} equivariant principal bundle
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivariantConnectedComponentsOfEquivariantClassifyingSpaces"}
            below) where
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semidirect+product+groups"} semidirect product groups
            appear as
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+groups"} equivariant groups
          %p
            In particular (Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GroupoidOfCrossedHomorphismsIsSlicedFunctorGroupoid"}
            below, which is not made explicit in traditional literature):
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+coefficient+bundle"} local coefficient bundle
                for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+cohomology"} non-abelian
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
                in degree-1 is the image of the projection out of the semidirect product group under forming
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping+groupoids"} delooping groupoids
            %li
              %p
                the
                = succeed "-theoretic" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+%282%2C1%29-category"} strict (2,1)-category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
                of this bundle form precisely the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
                of crossed homomorphisms with “crossed conjugations” (Def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjointActionOnCrossedHomomorphisms"}
                below) between them;
            %li
              %p
                and the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
                of these groupoids is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+cohomology"} non-abelian
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^1(G,\Gamma)
                (Rem.
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AsGroup1Cocycles"}
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AsCoboundariesInGroupCohomology"}
          %p
            This last fact is widely appreciated (see Rem.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReferencesForNonabelianCrossedHomomorphisms"}
            below) in the special case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            is an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
            with coefficients in degree 1.
          %p
            Beware that, while the notion of crossed homomorphisms makes sense for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+objects"} group objects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
